.TH DDCOLORD.TOML 5 2026-11-27 "ddcolord 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
ddcolord.toml \- ddcolord configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
A TOML file mapping monitors, and the values of their color mode feature, to
ICC profiles.
Unknown keys are an error, so a misspelt key fails to load instead of being
ignored.
Every ICC file is read at load time and must carry the ICC signature; a
missing file, or one that is not an ICC profile, is an error then, not at
the first mode switch.
.SH TOP LEVEL
.TP
.BR interval " (integer, default 3)"
Seconds between polls.
At least 1.
.TP
.B [[monitor]]
One table per monitor model.
The first entry that matches an output's EDID wins.
.SH MONITOR
.TP
.BR vendor " (string, required)"
EDID three-letter PNP manufacturer ID, for example
.BR BNQ .
.TP
.BR model " (string, required)"
EDID monitor name descriptor, for example
.BR "BenQ PD3220U" .
A monitor whose EDID has no name descriptor cannot be matched.
.TP
.BR serial " (string)"
EDID serial string, not empty.
Only needed to give two identical monitors different tables; when unset,
any serial matches.
.TP
.BR feature " (integer, default 0xdc)"
VCP feature code that reports the color mode.
MCCS calls 0xDC "Display Mode"; vendors fill its values with their own
mode numbers.
.TP
.BR unmapped " (path)"
Profile for a mode that has no
.B icc
of its own, and for a value not listed at all.
When unset, such a mode leaves the current profile in place.
.TP
.B [[monitor.mode]]
One table per mode.
.SH MODE
.TP
.BR code " (integer, required)"
Low byte (SL) of the feature's value.
.TP
.BR sub " (integer)"
High byte (SH).
An entry with
.B sub
matches only that value; one without matches any.
The exact match wins when both exist.
.TP
.BR name " (string, required)"
Used in logs and by
.BR "ddcolord \-\-probe" .
.TP
.BR icc " (path)"
ICC profile for this mode.
A relative path is relative to the config file's directory.
.SH NOTES
Monitors may answer a VCP code they do not implement with a copy of their
previous reply rather than an error.
ddcolord rejects a reply whose feature code differs from the one it asked
for, but a feature that is not declared in the monitor's capabilities
string
.RB ( "ddcutil capabilities" )
should not be configured.
.PP
colord ships sRGB, Adobe RGB (1998) and Rec.709 profiles among others, but
no Display P3 or DCI\-P3.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
interval = 3

[[monitor]]
vendor = "BNQ"
model = "BenQ PD3220U"
unmapped = "/usr/share/color/icc/colord/sRGB.icc"

[[monitor.mode]]
code = 0x0a
name = "sRGB"
icc = "/usr/share/color/icc/colord/sRGB.icc"

[[monitor.mode]]
code = 0x25
name = "Adobe RGB"
icc = "/usr/share/color/icc/colord/AdobeRGB1998.icc"

[[monitor.mode]]
code = 0x13
sub = 0x04
name = "Low Blue Light: Reading"
.fi
.PP
A complete table for the BenQ PD3220U ships as
.IR examples/benq\-pd3220u.toml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcolord (1)
